-#
-#  The core's flash message of one level, plus the level info (blue), which
-#  the core's layouts do not list: it shows right after notice, wherever
-#  notice is shown. The text goes through simple_format, which keeps safe
-#  tags (ul, li, code, img, a, ...) -- whatever a message takes from a user
-#  must come escaped. Each paragraph goes into a div, not a p as in the
-#  core: a p may not hold a list, a div may. The paragraphs are spaced as
-#  the core's p (customizable/_wagon.scss).
- levels = (level.to_sym == :notice) ? %i[notice info] : [level.to_sym]
- levels.each do |shown|
  - if flash[shown].present?
    - text = [flash[shown]].flatten.join("\n")
    %div{class: "alert alert-#{flash_class(shown)} alert-dismissible fade show"}
      %button.btn-close{type: :button, 'data-bs-dismiss': :alert, 'aria-label': t('global.button.close')}
      = simple_format(text, {}, wrapper_tag: "div")
